== 2. Closed forms / asymptotes ==
  OU (C) z=2.0: exact h*tau=3.6453e-02; Kramers asymptote 2z e^-z^2/sqrt(pi) (two-sided = 2x one-sided z e^-z^2/sqrt(pi)) = 4.1334e-02
  OU (C) z=3.0: exact h*tau=3.9089e-04; Kramers asymptote 2z e^-z^2/sqrt(pi) (two-sided = 2x one-sided z e^-z^2/sqrt(pi)) = 4.1776e-04
  OU (C) z=4.0: exact h*tau=4.9086e-07; Kramers asymptote 2z e^-z^2/sqrt(pi) (two-sided = 2x one-sided z e^-z^2/sqrt(pi)) = 5.0793e-07
  reset (B) z=2.0: h*tau=1.3353e-01; asymptote 2 e^(-sqrt2 z) = 1.1821e-01
  reset (B) z=3.0: h*tau=2.9583e-02; asymptote 2 e^(-sqrt2 z) = 2.8739e-02
  reset (B) z=4.0: h*tau=7.0361e-03; asymptote 2 e^(-sqrt2 z) = 6.9870e-03
  delay (A) z=2.0: h*tau=9.3150e-02; per-window P=9.1001e-02; 4*Phi(-z)(=2*erfc(z/sqrt2))=9.1001e-02
  delay (A) z=3.0: h*tau=5.4040e-03; per-window P=5.3996e-03; 4*Phi(-z)(=2*erfc(z/sqrt2))=5.3996e-03
  delay (A) z=4.0: h*tau=1.2669e-04; per-window P=1.2668e-04; 4*Phi(-z)(=2*erfc(z/sqrt2))=1.2668e-04
  one-sided fixed window (reflection principle): P(max_[0,tau] W >= B) = 2 Phi(-z) = erfc(z/sqrt2)

== 3. Monte Carlo validation (Brownian-bridge crossing correction) ==
  A z=0.5: MC MFPT/tau = 0.253 +- 0.003 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 0.250
  A z=1.0: MC MFPT/tau = 1.084 +- 0.015 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 1.112
  A z=1.5: MC MFPT/tau = 3.389 +- 0.050 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 3.400
  B z=0.5: MC MFPT/tau = 0.256 +- 0.003 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 0.261
  B z=1.0: MC MFPT/tau = 1.156 +- 0.015 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 1.178
  B z=1.5: MC MFPT/tau = 3.240 +- 0.045 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 3.231
  C z=0.5: MC MFPT/tau = 0.278 +- 0.004 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 0.272
  C z=1.0: MC MFPT/tau = 1.439 +- 0.020 (unabsorbed 0);  theory 1/F = 1.445
